
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pronouns.mgr - Japanese-pack first/second-person pronouns (Phase 8).
#
# v1 ships a small pronoun set:
#   私    - first-person, formal/neutral. Default for ?_I generation.
#   わたし - first-person, semi-formal (hiragana variant). Accepts on parse.
#   僕    - first-person, casual male. Accepts on parse; not used for
#            generation in v1 (gender-aware first-person is a follow-up,
#            shared shape with Swedish adjective gender agreement - see
#            dialogue_nlg_phase8_design.md section 8.10).
#   あなた - second-person. Japanese drops 2nd-person more than English, but
#            tell_about possessive forms ("your mother") need an explicit
#            possessor token; あなた fills that role.
#   これ / それ - this/that, ?_this binding.
#
# Possessive forms ("my X" / "your X") are not separate pronouns in Japanese -
# they are pronoun + の (no, the possessive particle). The NP templates in
# NounPhrases.mgr realize that compositionally rather than via a possessive
# pronoun lexeme; see "私 の $rel(REL)" there.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

:PRONOUN

"私"      ?_I     .
"わたし"   ?_I     .
"僕"      ?_I     .

"あなた"   ?_you   .

"これ"    ?_this  .
"それ"    ?_this  .
